  "result": "The core risk here is prompt injection: ticket text is customer-submitted free text, and it now drives a tool that can send real email and read every customer's order history \u2014 so a crafted ticket could trick the bot into emailing sensitive data to an attacker-controlled address, or drafting emails to other customers entirely. I'd recommend scoping DB access down to just the ticket's own customer record (not the full table) and treating send_email as needing a human-approval or allowlist gate before launch, even though that adds friction to legitimate \"look up related order\" cases.\n\nWant me to run a structured stress test against this \u2014 try a set of adversarial ticket payloads (injection, data exfiltration via email, cross-customer email misdirection) against the actual tool wiring and write up what happens and what's left unmitigated?",
